  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a permanently charged quaternary ammonium tropane ester; diphemanil methylsulphate, also a quaternary ammonium salt, showed very low oral bioavailability in healthy subjects after a 250 mg oral dose based on minimal urinary recovery, providing direct low-F evidence for this charge class.",
      "card_ids": ["C05"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Strongly cationic molecules can have F well below 20%: DX-9065 had human oral bioavailability of 2–3% (2.8 ± 1.5% for a conventional gelatin capsule; 3% for a fasted conventional capsule), attributed to its strong basic amidino groups.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C03", "C12"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics trospium and glycopyrrolate show only pg/mL plasma Cmax after milligram oral doses (trospium 60 mg XR Cmax 1517–1873 pg/mL; glycopyrrolate 2 mg Cmax 318 pg/mL), consistent with poor oral absorption and low F.",
      "card_ids": ["C28", "C34", "C35", "C38"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption/solubility/permeability records do not provide threshold-relevant permeability for the query: trospium chloride high aqueous solubility (>100 mg/mL) supports favorable dissolution but does not address the quaternary ammonium permeability barrier; atropine dissolution, ephedrine permeability, and ketoprofen/fenoprofen solubility/permeability records are not applicable due to different charge, scaffold, or acid class.",
      "card_ids": ["C40", "C41", "C42", "C43", "C44", "C45", "C46", "C47", "C48", "C49", "C50", "C51"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C40", "C41", "C42", "C43", "C44", "C45", "C46", "C47", "C48", "C49", "C50", "C51"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No matched oral versus intravenous exposure data are available for the query.",
    "No permeability or efflux measurement for a quaternary ammonium tropane is provided in L4; trospium solubility alone does not resolve the absorption barrier.",
    "Most L4 records are for structurally unrelated molecules (ketoprofen, fenoprofen, ephedrine, paeoniflorin) or for tertiary-amine atropine, limiting transferability.",
    "Differences in ester hydrolysis, metabolism, formulation, and dose between the query and cited quaternary ammonium analogs are unmeasured.",
    "No gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data are yet available for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: the query is a permanently charged quaternary ammonium tropane ester. Direct low-F evidence for the quaternary ammonium class (diphemanil, C05) and strongly cationic molecules (DX-9065, C01/C03/C12), plus pg/mL Cmax for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics trospium and glycopyrrolate (C28/C34/C35/C38), supports F < 20%. L4 adds mostly non-applicable solubility/permeability records; trospium high solubility (C49) does not overcome the permeability barrier. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query F measurement exists."
}

